Rules:
  [T1] Always use `strict: true` in tsconfig.json.
  [T2] Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases.
  [T3] Use `unknown` instead of `any` for unknown values.
  [T4] Use `readonly` for immutable properties.
  [T5] Use `enum` sparingly — prefer union types.
  [T6] Use `const` assertions for literal types.
  [T7] Use `as const` for readonly literal types.
  [T8] Enable `noImplicitAny` and `strictNullChecks`.

Pros:
  - Type safety
  - Better IDE support
  - Catches bugs at compile time

Cons:
  - Compilation overhead
  - Learning curve
  - Verbose for simple scripts

Alternatives:
  - JavaScript (simpler)
  - Flow (alternative)
  - JSDoc (lightweight)

State: +

